  "iconUrl": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
  "name": "Calculate3DVector",
  "previewIconUrl": "",
  "shortDescription": "3D vector math expressions: build vectors from distance and angles, camera forward/right vectors, normalize, dot/cross product, angles and distances. Designed to work with A3F.",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": [
    "3D vector expressions for GDevelop, consistent with the A3F extension:  ",
    "- Vec3_X / Vec3_Y / Vec3_Z: vector from distance, Z angle and X angle (camera convention)",
    "- CameraForward / CameraRight: vectors from the camera rotation, no -90 offset needed",
    "- Length, Normalize, Distance, Dot, Cross, AngleBetween, AngleZ, AngleX",
    "- DistanceToPoint: distance from a 3D object to a position (center or origin point)",
    "",
    "Angles are in degrees. Z angle: 0 = +X, 90 = +Y. X angle: 0 = down, 90 = horizontal, 180 = up (same as the 3D camera RotationX)."
  ],
  "tags": [
    "3d",
    "vector",
    "math",
    "camera",
    "direction",
    "distance",
    "angle"
  ],
